# Copy or adapt this example only after selecting the project's actual variables.
# Declare their names, types, required contexts and secret classification in
# config/environment.json. Backbone tooling itself requires no application secrets.
# Keep actual local values in the ignored .env file or a task-scoped secret store.
# The checker reads .env only with --env-file; it does not configure your app loader.
# Never place real API keys, tokens, passwords or production credentials here.
